  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Represent the solution of the inequality $a+5\\ge 11$ on a number line.",
  "worked_solution": "To isolate $a,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *adding* $5,$ which is *subtracting* $5.$\nRemember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+5 & \\ge 11 \\\\ a+5-5 & \\ge 11-5 \\\\ a+0 & \\ge 6 \\\\ a & \\ge 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a\\ge 6.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192536/assets/7d898136f9b5ad8adfb0b2354c3b7b9630c7270440fafb481fbc860ee4fcc627.png)",
